/E (Own your morning: as soon as you wake up, be mindful and intentional with what you do. The practice you do before you sleep \(Principle 1\) and the own your morning practice are like a relay, they work hand in hand. The ideas and feelings you had as you went to sleep are to be continued in the morning through solitude or not allowing any negative ideas into your mind. Owning your morning principle continues the state you were in as you went to sleep the night before. This \(owning your morning principle\) justifies the state you imagined; whatever you imagine will always, without fail, be manifested in your reality.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [2]
